      <data key="d0">Tax Bracket</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">A tax bracket refers to a range of income that is taxed at a specific rate, affecting the value of deductions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP">
      <data key="d0">RRSP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RRSP stands for Registered Retirement Savings Plan, a tax-advantaged savings account for retirement in Canada.&lt;SEP&gt;Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) is a retirement savings plan that provides tax advantages for Canadians saving for retirement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101362</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Higher Tax Bracket">
      <data key="d0">Higher Tax Bracket</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Being in a higher tax bracket refers to a status where individuals have higher income levels and therefore pay taxes at a greater rate.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Income Splitting">
      <data key="d0">Income Splitting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Income splitting is a tax strategy that allows couples to reduce their overall tax burden by distributing income between partners.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101328</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax-Deferred Growth">
      <data key="d0">Tax-Deferred Growth</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax-deferred growth is the increase in value of an investment that grows without being taxed until withdrawals are made.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-74f42f89274db1c03e3ad487f53119a4</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Registered Retirement Savings Plan">
      <data key="d0">Registered Retirement Savings Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Registered Retirement Savings Plan (RRSP) is a tax-advantaged savings plan registered with the Canada Revenue Agency, allowing for tax-deductible contributions and tax-deferred investment growth.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Revenue Agency">
      <data key="d0">Canada Revenue Agency</data>
      <data key="d1">organization</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Revenue Agency (CRA) is the governmental body responsible for tax collection and administration in Canada, overseeing Registered Retirement Savings Plans.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101329</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP Deduction Limit">
      <data key="d0">RRSP Deduction Limit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RRSP deduction limit defines the maximum amount an individual can deduct for RRSP contributions in a tax year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101330</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Year 2020">
      <data key="d0">Tax Year 2020</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax Year 2020 refers to the year for which the RRSP maximum new room limit was set at $27,230.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101330</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Year 2021">
      <data key="d0">Tax Year 2021</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax Year 2021 refers to the year for which the RRSP maximum new room limit was set at $27,830.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101330</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Year 2022">
      <data key="d0">Tax Year 2022</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax Year 2022 refers to the year for which the RRSP maximum new room limit was set at $29,210.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101330</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Tax Year 2023">
      <data key="d0">Tax Year 2023</data>
      <data key="d1">event</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax Year 2023 refers to the year for which the RRSP maximum new room limit was set at $30,780.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101331</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Overcontribution Penalty">
      <data key="d0">Overcontribution Penalty</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Overcontribution Penalty is a tax applied to contributions exceeding the RRSP deduction limit by more than $2,000, accrues monthly until corrected.&lt;SEP&gt;The overcontribution penalty applies when contributions exceed the allowed TFSA limit, resulting in a 1% tax per month on the excess amount.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4efa231cfe20987fec08d6db7e701fb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101401</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Form T1-OVP">
      <data key="d0">Form T1-OVP</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">Form T1-OVP is the Individual Tax Return for RRSP, PRPP, and SPP Excess Contributions, which must be filed when overcontributions occur.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101331</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Spousal RRSP">
      <data key="d0">Spousal RRSP</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Spousal RRSP allows an individual to contribute to their spouse's or common-law partner's RRSP, providing tax deductions while the spouse owns the plan.&lt;SEP&gt;Spousal RRSP is a type of RRSP that allows one spouse to contribute to the other's retirement savings to equalize tax burdens during retirement.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101362</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Home Buyers' Plan">
      <data key="d0">Home Buyers' Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Home Buyers' Plan (HBP) permits first-time home buyers to withdraw certain funds from their RRSP tax-free to purchase or build a qualifying home.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101332</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Lifelong Learning Plan">
      <data key="d0">Lifelong Learning Plan</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Lifelong Learning Plan (LLP) allows for RRSP withdrawals for education or training expenses, subject to repayment requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101332</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP Withdrawals">
      <data key="d0">RRSP Withdrawals</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RRSP Withdrawals are amounts taken from an RRSP, which are generally taxed as income when received.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101332</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP at Death">
      <data key="d0">RRSP at Death</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The RRSP at Death refers to the treatment of an RRSP following the account holder's death, potentially rolling over to a qualifying survivor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101333</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Key Tax Planning Strategies">
      <data key="d0">Key Tax Planning Strategies</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Key Tax Planning Strategies with RRSPs include maximizing deductions by contributing in higher tax brackets and utilizing spousal RRSPs for income splitting.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101333</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRSP Contribution Limits">
      <data key="d0">RRSP Contribution Limits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">RRSP Contribution Limits describe the calculations for the maximum deductible amount for contributions made to a Registered Retirement Savings Plan in a given year.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101333</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Annual RRSP Dollar Limits">
      <data key="d0">Annual RRSP Dollar Limits</data>
      <data key="d1">data</data>
      <data key="d2">Annual RRSP Dollar Limits represent the specific maximum contribution amounts set for each tax year from 2020 to 2025.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-1590b8716306682b296c39fb8f8a1c64</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101334</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Charitable Donation Tax Credit">
      <data key="d0">Charitable Donation Tax Credit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Charitable Donation Tax Credit is a tax incentive based on the fair market value of securities at the time of donation, promoting efficient giving strategies.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101360</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Work from Home Expenses">
      <data key="d0">Work from Home Expenses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Work from Home Expenses refer to the costs employees can deduct when required to work from home, including home office expenses.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101360</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Employment Deductions">
      <data key="d0">Employment Deductions</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Employment Deductions encompass various allowable expenses that employees can claim on their taxes based on their job requirements.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101360</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Vehicle Expenses">
      <data key="d0">Vehicle Expenses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Vehicle Expenses are deductions available to employees using personal vehicles for work-related tasks, including fuel and maintenance costs.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101360</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Medical Expenses">
      <data key="d0">Medical Expenses</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Medical Expenses are costs that can be claimed for tax credits, specifically for expenses exceeding certain thresholds within a 12-month period.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101361</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Form T2200">
      <data key="d0">Form T2200</data>
      <data key="d1">method</data>
      <data key="d2">Form T2200 is a tax form that certifies an employee's eligibility for claiming various work-related expenses, including those for work from home and vehicle usage.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101361</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Unused Donation Credits">
      <data key="d0">Unused Donation Credits</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Unused Donation Credits refer to charitable donation tax credits that can be carried forward up to 5 years for tax purposes.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101361</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="29%/33% Federal Credit Rate">
      <data key="d0">29%/33% Federal Credit Rate</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The 29%/33% Federal Credit Rate indicates the federal tax credit rates applicable under certain income conditions for charitable donations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-53761e82537ba7b2a5d7a74c8d5799d8</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101361</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canadian Tax Planning Strategies">
      <data key="d0">Canadian Tax Planning Strategies</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Canadian Tax Planning Strategies refer to various methods and approaches for optimizing tax liabilities in Canada, as outlined in CRA publications and the Income Tax Act.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101362</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="TFSA">
      <data key="d0">TFSA</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Tax-Free Savings Account (TFSA) is a savings account that allows Canadians to earn tax-free investment income and withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101363</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Capital Gains">
      <data key="d0">Capital Gains</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Capital gains are the profits made from selling an asset for more than its purchase price, which is subject to tax regulations.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101363</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Pension Income Splitting">
      <data key="d0">Pension Income Splitting</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Pension income splitting allows individuals receiving qualifying pension income to allocate part of their income to their spouse for tax benefits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101363</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Canada Child Benefit">
      <data key="d0">Canada Child Benefit</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">The Canada Child Benefit (CCB) is a government program that provides financial support to families with children based on their family income.&lt;SEP&gt;The Canada Child Benefit is a financial support program for families with children, which is also not affected by TFSA withdrawals.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-4efa231cfe20987fec08d6db7e701fb2</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101403</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Charitable Donation">
      <data key="d0">Charitable Donation</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Charitable donations involve giving to registered charities, which can provide tax credits and other financial benefits to the donor.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101364</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="RRIF">
      <data key="d0">RRIF</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Registered Retirement Income Fund (RRIF) is a type of account that individuals must withdraw from in retirement and is influenced by previous RRSP contributions.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101364</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="OAS Clawback">
      <data key="d0">OAS Clawback</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Old Age Security (OAS) clawback refers to the reduction of OAS payments based on the recipient's income over a certain threshold.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101364</data>
      <data key="d6" />
    </node>
    <node id="Capital Gains Reserve">
      <data key="d0">Capital Gains Reserve</data>
      <data key="d1">concept</data>
      <data key="d2">Capital Gains Reserve allows individuals to claim a capital gain over several years for property sold with deferred payments, subject to specific time limits.</data>
      <data key="d3">chunk-443ee4b9b0cd32b4e6c22127239ed83c</data>
      <data key="d4">unknown_source</data>
      <data key="d5">1772101365</data>
